# Help: The mq-deadline, Kyber and BFQ multiqueue I/O schedulers
#
# mq-deadline defaults to y, which an allnoconfig-based merge drops, so
# it is set like the other two. BFQ keeps an I/O context per process
# and queue (BLK_ICQ, which it selects), so with it the block layer's
# io-context code is built too.
#
# builtin/storage/iosched.config builds all three into the kernel.
# See: block/Kconfig.iosched
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/block/bfq-iosched.html
CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEADLINE=m
CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_KYBER=m
CONFIG_IOSCHED_BFQ=m
